title: '[pallet-revive]: Add Versioning Macros'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    # Description

    Part of https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/11923 and closes https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/11945

    This PR introduces the procedural macro infrastructure needed for pallet-revive versioning work.

    It adds two macros to `pallet-revive-proc-macro`:

    - `define_versioned_type!`, for declaring versioned structs and enums while allowing later versions
      to be expressed as deltas from earlier versions.
    - `define_versioned_interface!`, for declaring paired versioned runtime API input/output payload
      families and generating the boxed versioned payload enums around them.

    This PR only adds the macro infrastructure. It does not introduce the new pallet-revive storage
    models, runtime API payload crate, runtime API functions, migrations, or execution/wire conversion
    logic. Those are intended to land in later PRs.

    ## Integration

    Downstream users do not need to change any existing pallet-revive code for this PR.

    The only new public surface is in `pallet-revive-proc-macro`. Consumers may opt into the new macros
    when they start defining versioned pallet-revive types or runtime API payloads.

    The proc-macro crate now has a `std` feature enabled by default. Crates that depend on
    `pallet-revive-proc-macro` from `no_std` contexts should disable default features and enable the
    macro crate's `std` feature only from their own `std` feature.

    This PR also updates `pallet-revive` and `pallet-revive-uapi` to depend on
    `pallet-revive-proc-macro` with `default-features = false`, then wires the macro crate's `std`
    feature through their own `std` feature lists.

    ## Review Notes

    > [!TIP]
    > The doc-comments for the two new macros that we added describe their functionality in great details and might be the best place to understand what these macros do, what they don't, and how they work. Consider reviewing that when reviewing this PR.

    `define_versioned_type!` accepts ordinary Rust struct and enum items whose names end in `V{N}`. It
    parses the base name and version, rejects malformed or non-contiguous version families, and emits
    full standalone Rust items for every version.

    The macro supports:

    - struct and enum versions;
    - versions that do not start at `V1`, as long as the declared range is contiguous;
    - type-level `#[versioned_type(extend)]`;
    - variant-level `#[versioned_type(extend)]` and `#[versioned_type(override)]`;
    - field-level `#[versioned_type(override)]`;
    - generated `Latest{Name}` aliases for the highest version;
    - diagnostics for duplicate versions, mixed base names, invalid helper attributes, unsupported
      extension shapes, and accidental field/variant redefinitions.

    `define_versioned_interface!` accepts only named-field structs following this naming scheme:

    ```rust
    {Name}InputPayloadV{N}
    {Name}OutputPayloadV{N}
    ```

    It emits:

    - the original payload structs unchanged;
    - `Versioned{Name}InputPayload`;
    - `Versioned{Name}OutputPayload`;
    - boxed `V{N}` variants;
    - constructors, accessors, consuming accessors, unwrap helpers, `From`, and `TryFrom` impls;
    - `Latest{Name}InputPayload` and `Latest{Name}OutputPayload` aliases;
    - `LATEST_VERSION` constants on generated versioned enums.

    If the payload family name ends with `Versioned`, the generated enum and alias names strip that
    marker. For example, `EthTransactVersionedInputPayloadV1` generates
    `VersionedEthTransactInputPayload`, not `VersionedEthTransactVersionedInputPayload`.

    The existing `define_env` macro implementation is also moved into its own handler module so the
    proc-macro crate follows the same file layout as the new versioning macros.

    Tests cover both normal expansion and compile-fail behavior, including trybuild UI tests for invalid
    macro input.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive-proc-macro
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive-uapi
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-sdk
  bump: patch
